{
  "name": "Self-Maintaining Cell \u2014 boundary, turnover, repair, viability",
  "description": "Fig 8 (self-organized processes) mechanistic variant. A self-maintaining cell on a replenished medium: a membrane GATES nutrient import, metabolism (enzyme-catalysed) makes ATP + precursors, and precursor+ATP are spent to synthesise enzymes and REPAIR the membrane; every component degrades (turnover), so persistence requires continuous replacement. The cell grows to a far-from-equilibrium STEADY STATE, a one-time membrane injury at tick 45 is REPAIRED and viability RECOVERS. Operational closure: each component is produced by processes that depend on that component. Mechanism knockouts (k_transport/k_met/k_expr/k_repair\u2192epsilon) and a non-replenished medium each collapse viability \u2014 dependence. This does NOT establish autopoiesis in the strong sense (the boundary is a scalar area, the viability target is scripted).",
  "default_n_steps": 90,
  "requires": {
    "processes": [
      "NutrientReservoir",
      "SelfMaintainingCell"
    ]
  },
